Subject: [PATCH 4/4] storage: offer the app-private directory as a one-tap
 storage location

Anikku already falls back to Android/data/<package>/files/<app name> when
no SAF folder picker is available (Fire TV). Expose that location as an
explicit choice:

- Settings > Data and storage: a "Use app-private storage" entry below the
  storage location picker (disabled once it is active).
- Onboarding storage step: a second button next to "Select folder".

The directory is a plain filesystem path, so UniFile works on java.io.File
and neither ffmpeg-kit's SAF protocol nor renameDocument() is involved -
both are broken on HarmonyOS ZhuoyiTong. Gallery apps never index
Android/data, which is the second reason HarmonyOS users want it. The
trade-off (contents are removed when the app is uninstalled) is stated in
the summary text.

Strings are added to i18n-ank (base + zh-rCN).
